  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the nets of each solid.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/277d5aa8a8116d230bf000ef7d8e94a071acbf499a49b9d8b911a4e89cfaf18a.png)\n\n \n\nAs we can see, the correct answer is:\n\n$\\,$ *\"The net of II consists of triangles only\"*\n\nOther statements are false. \n\n- *\"The net of III consists of triangles only\"* is false since the net of III has one rectangle (the base of the solid).\n\n- *\"The net of I consists of $3$ triangles and $3$ rectangles\"* is not true because the net of I contains only $2$ triangles (the base and the top of the solid).\n\n- *\"The net of III consists of $3$ triangles and $1$ rectangle\"* is false since the net of III has $4$ triangles (the side faces).\n\n- *\"The net of II consists of $3$ triangles and $1$ rectangle\"* is not true because the net of II does not contain rectangles.",
